{"episodes":{"177629":"Cool, unstable air mass moved across the region resulting in reports of small hail and one report of a funnel cloud.","178771":"Scattered strong to severe thunderstorms produced a few reports of large hail and flash flooding across portions of the Big Country.","178856":"An upper level disturbance interacted with moisture overriding a stalled front over Arkansas to produce showers and a few thunderstorms over the area from the afternoon of the 7th to the early morning of the 8th. While most of the area received between one-quarter to one-half inch of rain, locations along Interstate 44 from Joplin to Springfield and along Highway 60 from Springfield to Cabool received over one and a half inches. Isolated reports of flooding were received from Lawrence, Douglas and Wright counties where soils were already saturated from heavy rain earlier in the month.","178977":"Isolated thunderstorms which developed across western portions of North Texas produced marginally severe hail in a few instances."},"events":[{"begin":"2023-03-08T00:55Z","county":"Washington","deaths":0,"end":"2023-03-08T00:55Z","endLat":45.4449,"endLon":-123.1376,"episode":177629,"id":1080321,"injuries":0,"lat":45.4434,"location":"1 NNW Gaston","lon":-123.1379,"magnitude":0.75,"narrative":"Hail size of 0.75 inch was estimated from picture posted on social media.","source":"Social Media","state":"OR","type":"Hail","wfo":"PQR"},{"begin":"2023-03-08T02:06Z","county":"Washington","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-03-08T02:06Z","endLat":45.4084,"endLon":-123.0536,"episode":177629,"id":1080320,"injuries":0,"lat":45.4079,"location":"4 ESE Gaston","lon":-123.0538,"narrative":"Picture showing what appears to be a narrow funnel cloud near Bald Peak Road in Washington County.","source":"Social Media","state":"OR","type":"Funnel Cloud","wfo":"PQR"},{"begin":"2023-03-08T11:44Z","county":"Lawrence","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":